## How the desk should triage now

Look up the tenant and booking form, read the body, and compare the failing path before merging. Same subject can hide different causes; different subjects can describe one cause. A missing tenant is insufficient evidence to merge. Read [the revised triage guide](/kb/triage/dedupe) and [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause); the accepted old decision remains as history.

<DedupeExplorer />

## What remains uncertain

The cause table is an assignment rule, not a reproduction of the product bug. The desk-note reports above need direct investigation; one even describes an invite predating its booking. Capture intended date, stored date, timestamps, timezone, form and the received invite. Do not mark them resolved without checking their actual behavior.

This review does not deploy a product fix. Keep both engineering issues open until their acceptance checks pass, and review incoming reports because the desk continues working after this export.

